course: dictionary
lesson: 14160
title: Mistreated: when someone is treated badly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mistreated means treated badly, cruelly or unfairly. The word begins with mis-, which shows something went wrong, and it comes from the verb mistreat, which means to treat someone or something badly.
explain: «The old dog was mistreated by its owner, who left it out in the cold with no food.» The clues are left out in the cold and no food. A good dog should be looked after, so mistreated must mean treated badly and not cared for.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «treated well» instead of mistreated: «The dog was treated well by its owner» does not fit the clues, so you know mistreated means the opposite. Children can also feel mistreated, as in «Sam felt mistreated when he was blamed for something he did not do.»
explain: If you or a friend is being hurt or neglected, tell a trusted adult straight away. You can also call a helpline, such as Childline in the UK. Telling someone is brave, and it is never your fault.
fact: Mistreated means treated badly, cruelly or unfairly.
fact: Mistreated can also mean harmed or neglected, as with animals or children who are not cared for properly.
fact: Useful phrases: mistreated animals, felt mistreated, badly mistreated.
fact: No child or animal should be mistreated. Mistreating animals is a crime.
fact: In stories, mistreated characters such as Cinderella and Harry Potter at the Dursleys' are often shown finding kindness at last.
exercise: «The farmer was caught mistreating his animals, so the police took them away.» What does mistreating mean? | Painting them bright colours | *Treating badly and cruelly | Feeding them every day | Taking them for a long walk
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means treated badly: «Cinderella felt mistreated, but one day she found kindness.» | Cinderella | kindness | *mistreated | found
exercise: Ella said, «Nobody should be mistreated, so I told my teacher.» Why did Ella tell her teacher? | To say hello to her friend | *Because someone was being hurt or neglected | Because she was bored in class | To get a sweet from the teacher
test: «Harry Potter was mistreated by the Dursleys until he found a home at Hogwarts.» What does mistreated mean here? | *Treated badly and unfairly | Given a new name | Taken on a holiday | Treated like a king
test: If someone is being hurt or neglected, what should you do? | Wait and hope it stops by itself | Hide and say nothing to anyone | *Tell a trusted adult or call a helpline such as Childline | Keep it secret forever
exam: Which word fits best? «The hungry cat was ___ when nobody gave it food or water.» | ancient | delighted | luminous | *mistreated
